record jpegxl-rs.work.arch-phase35-lane-batched-dct/1 : work {
    title "Phase 35: lane-batched separable DCT kernels and cached ScaleF"
    state completed
    scope [
        path ".agent/scratch/**",
        path "JPXL/crates/jpxl-core/src/dct.rs",
        path "JPXL/crates/jpxl-core/src/forward.rs",
        path "JPXL/crates/jpxl-core/src/varblock.rs",
        path "JPXL/docs/optimize.md"
    ]
    intent """
        A fresh P-core profile of the Balanced 1-bpp mid encode after Phase 34 attributes roughly 19% of self time to the separable DCT family (dct_2d_in_place 4.1%, dct_1d 3.8%, forward_dct_rc 3.4%, dct_iv_16 2.5%, dct_iv_8 1.9%, dct_ii_32 1.7%, lf_from_llf_into 1.4%) plus 0.9% to libm cos reached through I.8 ScaleF, which recomputes three f64 cosines per LLF cell on every call. The 1-D kernels are per-vector scalar (the simd feature only shuffles one 8-vector through f32x4), and every 2-D pass transposes so scalar kernels can run on contiguous rows. Make the 1-D kernels generic over a lane type (f32, and wide f32x4/f32x8 under simd) so one implementation transforms one column per lane, drive both DCT_2D and IDCT_2D with lane-batched column passes (dropping one transpose from the forward direction), cache ScaleF for the tabled power-of-two LF counts, and copy varblock rows in bulk in forward_dct_rc. Every lane executes exactly the scalar op sequence (no FMA, no reassociation), so encoder and decoder output must remain byte-identical for the simd and no-simd builds; promotion requires canonical stream identity across presets and thread counts, decoder-side conformance and roundtrip suites unchanged, external decoder acceptance, a reduced DCT-family profile share, and non-regressing pinned wall time.
        """
    note """
        Opened 2026-08-17 from a fresh perf profile (.agent/scratch/phase35-lane-dct/baseline-mid.perf.data) taken on the Phase 34 head binary.
        """
    acceptance {
        check identity {
            statement """
                Canonical Fast, Balanced, and Quality streams on mid and large inputs, plus one-thread/four-thread Balanced outputs, are byte-identical to the Phase 34 head binary; the lane-batched kernels equal the scalar kernels bit-for-bit under property tests over every supported shape.
                """
            method command
            verified_by [ @jpegxl-rs.evidence.phase35-identity-2026-08-17/1 ]
        }
        check safety {
            statement """
                Workspace fmt, build, strict Clippy, and the full test suite pass with default features and with jpxl-core simd disabled; decoder conformance/oracle suites pass; the canonical candidate decodes through vendored djxl and jxl-oxide.
                """
            method command
            verified_by [ @jpegxl-rs.evidence.phase35-safety-2026-08-17/1 ]
        }
        check speed {
            statement """
                A fresh perf profile shows the DCT-family self-time share reduced materially from the ~19% baseline, and pinned four-core Balanced 1-bpp mid/large medians do not regress.
                """
            method observation
            verified_by [ @jpegxl-rs.evidence.phase35-speed-2026-08-17/1 ]
        }
    }
    depends_on [ @jpegxl-rs.work.arch-phase34-indexed-lane4-cfl/1 ]
    part_of [ @jpegxl-rs.track.encoder-optimization ]
}

record jpegxl-rs.work.arch-phase36-runtime-avx2-row-quantizer/1 : work {
    title "Phase 36: runtime AVX2 dispatch and the row-oriented lane quantizer"
    state completed
    scope [
        path ".agent/scratch/**",
        path "JPXL/crates/jpxl-core/src/cpu.rs",
        path "JPXL/crates/jpxl-core/src/dct.rs",
        path "JPXL/crates/jpxl-core/src/lib.rs",
        path "JPXL/crates/jpxl-core/src/simd.rs",
        path "JPXL/crates/jpxl-encode-policy/src/lib.rs",
        path "JPXL/crates/jpxl-encode-policy/src/quantize.rs",
        path "JPXL/docs/optimize.md"
    ]
    intent """
        The user asked for AVX2 to be the default whenever the host supports it. The workspace compiles for baseline x86-64, so wide's f32x8 is two SSE registers, and LLVM does not re-widen it inside a #[target_feature(enable = "avx2")] function (verified in the disassembly: the wrapper had 2,418 xmm and zero ymm arithmetic instructions). Add jpxl_core::cpu::has_avx2 (cached std::arch detection, JPXL_DISABLE_AVX2 opt-out for A/B) and jpxl_core::simd::F32Vec, one lane trait with a scalar f32 implementation, wide f32x4/f32x8 implementations, and a __m256-backed simd::avx2::F32x8 whose contract is documented at the type and is the only unsafe in the tree; kernels are written once against the trait and instantiated a second time inside a target-feature entry point that callers reach only after has_avx2. Apply it to the Phase 35 DCT column pass and, more importantly, to the HF quantizer: replace the per-four-cell choose_lane4 calls in quantize_lane, cover scoring (score_channel_lanes) and the CfL luma walk with a row-oriented choose_run that hoists per-channel setup once and quantizes eight cells per AVX2 chunk with a padded final chunk instead of scalar tails, and give the CfL factor pricing an indexed choose_cells sibling. Every lane performs the scalar rule's IEEE operations in the scalar order (no FMA), a chunk that would fail replays the scalar loop so errors and cutoff order are exact, and both cover scoring and factor pricing fall back to their scalar per-cell loops when a run reports failure. Promotion requires canonical stream identity across presets, thread counts, the AVX2-on/off paths and the no-SIMD build; the full gate suite; and a reduced quantizer/DCT profile share with non-regressing pinned wall time.
        """
    note """
        Opened 2026-08-17 immediately after Phase 35 at the user's request (AVX2 default when available). Timing on this host is contaminated by concurrent builds (load average up to 90); the identity and profile-share evidence carry the correctness and cost claims, and pinned wall time is reported with its noise.
        """
    acceptance {
        check identity {
            statement """
                Canonical Fast/Balanced/Quality/masking-AQ/lossless streams on mid and large inputs, one- vs four-thread outputs, JPXL_DISABLE_AVX2 vs AVX2 outputs, and the no-SIMD build are all byte-identical to the Phase 35 binary; the F32Vec implementations, the run/indexed quantizer kernels and the lane DCT are pinned bit-identical to their scalar references by unit tests at every lane width available on the host.
                """
            method command
            verified_by [ @jpegxl-rs.evidence.phase36-identity-2026-08-17/1 ]
        }
        check safety {
            statement """
                Workspace fmt, build, strict Clippy and the full test suite pass with default features and with SIMD disabled; unsafe is confined to jpxl_core::simd::avx2 (type-level contract) plus the target-feature call sites; oracle, roundtrip and determinism suites pass; the candidates decode through djxl and jxl-oxide.
                """
            method command
            verified_by [ @jpegxl-rs.evidence.phase36-safety-2026-08-17/1 ]
        }
        check speed {
            statement """
                The AVX2 entry points demonstrably emit 256-bit arithmetic, a fresh profile shows the choose/quantizer and DCT families reduced from the Phase 35 shares, and pinned four-core Balanced medians do not regress (reported with host-noise caveat).
                """
            method observation
            verified_by [ @jpegxl-rs.evidence.phase36-speed-2026-08-17/1 ]
        }
    }
    depends_on [ @jpegxl-rs.work.arch-phase35-lane-batched-dct/1 ]
    part_of [ @jpegxl-rs.track.encoder-optimization ]
}

record jpegxl-rs.work.arch-phase37-avx2-exact-cbrt-xyb/1 : work {
    title "Phase 37: exact AVX2 cube root and planar XYB conversion"
    state completed
    scope [
        path ".agent/scratch/**",
        path "JPXL/crates/jpxl-core/src/color.rs",
        path "JPXL/crates/jpxl-core/src/simd.rs",
        path "JPXL/docs/optimize.md"
    ]
    intent """
        After Phase 36 the largest scalar leaf in the Balanced profile was compiler_builtins' portable cbrtf (4.3%) plus the planar XYB conversion around it (1.7%). Reproduce that exact algorithm (5-bit integer estimate, two f64 Newton steps in the scalar operation order, one rounding to f32) as simd::avx2::F32x8::cbrt on 256-bit registers, declining chunks that hold the scalar special cases so the caller falls back to f32::cbrt there, and run the planar linear-sRGB-to-XYB conversion eight pixels at a time on F32x8 behind cpu::has_avx2. Bit-identity to f32::cbrt and to the single-pixel conversion is pinned by unit tests; canonical streams must stay byte-identical; the workspace gates must stay green.
        """
    note """
        Records the closure trap: intrinsics inside a closure in an #[inline(always)] body do not inherit the AVX2 target feature and become out-of-line calls (measured 60% slower before the fix).
        """
    acceptance {
        check identity {
            statement """
                F32x8::cbrt equals f32::cbrt bit for bit on the tested normal inputs and declines the special cases; the planar conversion equals the single-pixel function bitwise on every host path; canonical streams remain byte-identical to Phase 36 with AVX2 on and off.
                """
            method command
            verified_by [ @jpegxl-rs.evidence.phase37-identity-2026-08-17/1 ]
        }
        check safety {
            statement """
                fmt, build, strict Clippy, the 57 workspace suites, oracle/roundtrip/determinism, no-SIMD and AVX2-disabled suites pass.
                """
            method command
            verified_by [ @jpegxl-rs.evidence.phase37-safety-2026-08-17/1 ]
        }
        check speed {
            statement """
                The colour-conversion profile share drops materially and pinned Balanced medians do not regress.
                """
            method observation
            verified_by [ @jpegxl-rs.evidence.phase37-speed-2026-08-17/1 ]
        }
    }
    depends_on [ @jpegxl-rs.work.arch-phase36-runtime-avx2-row-quantizer/1 ]
    part_of [ @jpegxl-rs.track.encoder-optimization ]
}

record jpegxl-rs.work.arch-phase38-band-parallel-cfl-prep/1 : work {
    title "Phase 38: band-parallel CfL collection/refinement and source prep, narrowed pass-group walks, fast-debug profile"
    state completed
    scope [
        path ".agent/scratch/**",
        path "AGENTS.md",
        path "JPXL/Cargo.toml",
        path "JPXL/crates/jpxl-encode-policy/src/lib.rs",
        path "JPXL/crates/jpxl-encode-policy/src/rate.rs",
        path "JPXL/crates/jpxl-encode-policy/src/source.rs",
        path "JPXL/crates/jpxl-encode/src/vardct/write.rs",
        path "JPXL/docs/optimize.md"
    ]
    intent """
        The --diag phase clock after Phase 37 showed cfl_ms=103 of a 470 ms mid encode while CfL's CPU share was ~12%: HF factor refinement ran on the calling thread and sample collection parallelised only over LF groups (two on a 2400x1800 frame), and PreparedFrame::from_srgb8 ran serially before the executor existed. Split CfL collection into 64-pixel tile-row bands (varblocks are <=32 px, 8-aligned and raster ordered, so bands are independent and concatenate to the original order), run HF factor refinement over the executor per tile in order, build the worker pool once in encode_srgb8_to_target and use it for band-parallel from_srgb8_with, start pass_group_walk at the group's first tile row via partition_point instead of scanning the whole LF group per pass group, copy interior squares row-wise in gather_square, and add the fast-debug Cargo profile for the edit/test loop. All Contract A: byte-identical output required across presets, thread counts and AVX2 on/off. An ANS reciprocal/branchless rewrite was tried, measured no gain (the serial state chain is bound by the slot-table load) and reverted.
        """
    note """
        Opened 2026-08-17. Timing evidence records the shared-host caveat; identity and --diag phase clocks carry the claims.
        """
    acceptance {
        check identity {
            statement """
                Canonical Fast/Balanced/Quality/masking-AQ/lossless streams on mid and large inputs, one- vs four-thread outputs, and JPXL_DISABLE_AVX2 outputs are byte-identical to the Phase 37 binary.
