record jpegxl-rs.work.arch-phase40-cover-scoring-pass/1 : work {
    title "Phase 40: cheapen the single cover-scoring pass (row targets, direct luma reconstruction sink, per-row cutoff)"
    state completed
    scope [
        path ".agent/scratch/**",
        path "JPXL/crates/jpxl-encode-policy/src/lib.rs",
        path "JPXL/docs/optimize.md"
    ]
    intent """
        The planning review found no module needing an overhaul: cover, CfL and entropy training already run once per encode and the controller's data dependency keeps the quantize replays sequential under Contract A. The remaining planning-side lever is instruction volume in the one cover-scoring pass (cover_ms 123 of ~400 ms on mid), whose hot loop is score_channel_lanes inside block_cost_bounded. Rewrite it to take targets as LaneTargets (Y plane directly; chroma residual plane - k*d_y computed per row as a vectorisable zip), write the luma reconstruction straight into the caller's d_y_hf through the run kernel's reconstruction output, fold lambda*to_sample_domain once under the flat policy (per-cell weight exactly 1.0), and test the cutoff once per row instead of per cell -- decision-preserving because both accumulators only grow with non-negative finite terms and a pruned candidate is discarded whole; the scalar fallback keeps the per-cell order. Byte-identical output required.
        """
    note """
        Opened 2026-08-17 from the plan-mode review (two independent analyses). Host carried other jobs during measurement, so the cost claim uses load-independent perf stat instruction counts.
        """
    acceptance {
        check identity {
            statement """
                Canonical streams across presets, sizes, thread counts and AVX2 on/off are byte-identical to Phase 39.
                """
            method command
            verified_by [ @jpegxl-rs.evidence.phase40-identity-2026-08-17/1 ]
        }
        check safety {
            statement """
                fmt, strict Clippy, workspace suites in fast-debug and release, oracle/roundtrip/determinism, no-default-feature and AVX2-disabled suites pass.
                """
            method command
            verified_by [ @jpegxl-rs.evidence.phase40-safety-2026-08-17/1 ]
        }
        check speed {
            statement """
                perf stat instruction count for the mid Balanced bench drops materially, and the scoring symbols' instruction share drops.
                """
            method observation
            verified_by [ @jpegxl-rs.evidence.phase40-speed-2026-08-17/1 ]
        }
    }
    depends_on [ @jpegxl-rs.work.arch-phase39-lane-recon/1 ]
    part_of [ @jpegxl-rs.track.encoder-optimization ]
}

record jpegxl-rs.work.arch-phase41-hf-token-tape/1 : work {
    title "Phase 41: HF token tape -- one coefficient walk per written plan"
    state completed
    scope [
        path ".agent/scratch/**",
        path "JPXL/crates/jpxl-cli/src/main.rs",
        path "JPXL/crates/jpxl-encode-policy/src/rate.rs",
        path "JPXL/crates/jpxl-encode/Cargo.toml",
        path "JPXL/crates/jpxl-encode/src/vardct/diagnostics.rs",
        path "JPXL/crates/jpxl-encode/src/vardct/write.rs",
        path "JPXL/crates/jpxl-entropy/src/encode/ans.rs",
        path "JPXL/crates/jpxl-entropy/src/encode/mod.rs",
        path "JPXL/crates/jpxl-entropy/src/encode/stream.rs",
        path "JPXL/crates/jpxl-entropy/src/encode/tape.rs",
        path "JPXL/docs/optimize.md"
    ]
    intent """
        The writer walked each written plan's coefficients twice (build_entropy_tables into a dense TokenCensus, then write_pass_group into SymbolEncoder with per-symbol re-tokenization and a Vec<AnsSymbol> copy), 7 walks per encode. Add jpxl_entropy::encode::tape (TokenTapeRecorder / TokenTape): one walk per pass group tokenizes each event under its cluster's configuration, counts tokens per cluster (EntropyTables::build_from_token_counts is the split-out second half of build), and records a compact SoA tape that emission replays through encode_symbols_with and the same bit-writing sequence as SymbolEncoder::write_stream. Feature hf-token-tape (default on; off = two-walk oracle). Add the tape_symbols writer diagnostic. Byte-identical by construction and pinned by a unit test comparing tables and bytes with the replay encoder for clustered ANS and prefix plans.
        """
    note """
        Opened 2026-08-17 per the approved plan. Shared-host load prevented a clean wall measurement; instruction counts carry the cost claim, wall to be re-measured quiet.
        """
    acceptance {
        check identity {
            statement """
                Canonical streams across presets, sizes, thread counts and AVX2 on/off are byte-identical to Phase 40; the tape unit test proves tables and bytes equal the replay encoder's; djxl and jxl-oxide accept the candidates.
                """
            method command
            verified_by [ @jpegxl-rs.evidence.phase41-identity-2026-08-17/1 ]
        }
        check safety {
            statement """
                fmt, strict Clippy (both feature configurations of jpxl-encode), workspace suites in fast-debug and release, oracle/roundtrip/determinism, no-default-feature and AVX2-disabled suites pass.
                """
            method command
            verified_by [ @jpegxl-rs.evidence.phase41-safety-2026-08-17/1 ]
        }
        check speed {
            statement """
                Instruction count per mid Balanced bench drops materially; walks per encode drop from 7 to 4; tape memory measured via the tape_symbols diagnostic.
                """
            method observation
            verified_by [ @jpegxl-rs.evidence.phase41-speed-2026-08-17/1 ]
        }
    }
    depends_on [ @jpegxl-rs.work.arch-phase40-cover-scoring-pass/1 ]
    part_of [ @jpegxl-rs.track.encoder-optimization ]
}

