    part_of [ @jpegxl-rs.track.encoder-optimization ]
}

record jpegxl-rs.work.arch-phase4a-weighted-predictor-scoped/1 : work {
    title "Phase 4A: wire Predictor::Weighted into the encoder despite its stateful, order-dependent scoring cost"
    state completed
    intent """
        Wire the H.5 self-correcting predictor (now shared at jpxl_core::modular_weighted, moved from jpxl-decode) into jpxl-encode's predictor candidate list (crates/jpxl-encode/src/lossless.rs PREDICTOR_CANDIDATES, currently the six order-independent predictors: Zero, West, North, AverageWestNorth, Select, Gradient).

        COMPLICATION found while starting this (not present in the original scoping): every other candidate predictor is a pure function of neighbouring SAMPLE values, which is what let the encoder's residual-collection functions (collect_plane_residuals, and Phase 4B's collect_plane_residuals_sampled) be absolute-indexed and order-independent -- any row can be visited in any order or skipped. Predictor::Weighted (jpxl_core::modular_weighted::WeightedState) is stateful and ORDER-DEPENDENT: per H.5.1 it must be invoked for every sample of a channel in strict raster order, unconditionally, because its error state (used by the next sample's weight computation) accumulates across the whole scan and its max_error output is a context property. Confirmed in the decoder: jpxl-decode's per-channel loop constructs WeightedState once and calls predict/update on every sample regardless of which predictor a given leaf actually uses.

        Consequences for the encoder's scoring architecture (predictor sweep -> greedy split search -> per-leaf refinement -> exact final price, all documented in lossless.rs's module doc):
        1. Any candidate tree containing a Weighted leaf needs a full sequential O(pixels) scan to price, not a sampled scan (Phase 4B's row-strided sampling would corrupt the error state) and not one of the specialised single-leaf fast paths (Zero/West/North/Gradient in collect_plane_residuals).
        2. This full sequential scan is naturally scoped to TWO of the three search stages, not all three: (a) the initial per-predictor sweep (PREDICTOR_CANDIDATES tried as single_leaf trees, one full scan each -- Weighted becomes a 7th candidate here, no combinatorial blowup, same shape as today) and (b) per-leaf predictor refinement (also one full scan per candidate swap on the settled topology). It should NOT be added as a topology-search-time option inside the greedy split loop's O(leaves x properties x thresholds) inner loop -- but this may not need special-casing anyway, since split_leaf already carries the parent leaf's already-chosen predictor forward unchanged (lossless.rs: "same predictor both sides first (cheap topology search)"), so a Weighted-winning leaf from stage (a) propagates into splits for free without the split search itself needing to know about Weighted's cost model.
        3. Open question needing an explicit choice: does pricing a Weighted-containing candidate at stages (a)/(b) cost O(pixels) unconditionally (losing Phase 4B's speedup for just those specific trials, which is bounded and probably acceptable -- 7 trials in stage (a), <= leaves x 6 trials in stage (b)), or is there a cheaper still-safe way to rank it (e.g. a smaller fixed-size early-window sequential prefix, if that ranks predictors reliably enough -- needs its own decision-preservation proof if used, echoing the 4B regret-test pattern)?
        4. SPLIT_PROPERTIES (currently missing property 15, max_error) is a SEPARATE decision from adding the predictor itself -- property 15 is only informative once some sample in the channel actually runs Weighted, which after this change is universal (state runs on every sample, unconditionally, once ANY leaf might want it) -- IS the encoder already computing property 15 for every sample regardless of whether Weighted is a chosen predictor anywhere in the tree, matching the decoder's unconditional-invocation behaviour? If the encoder's per-candidate cost estimators don't currently run WeightedState at all (true today, since it's simply not called), then adding Weighted as a predictor candidate must ALSO start running WeightedState unconditionally across every trial from that point on (even Zero/West/etc-only trials) to keep property vectors correct if property 15 is ever split on -- or property 15 can stay excluded from SPLIT_PROPERTIES for this sub-phase, deferring context-splitting on max_error to a later increment, which shrinks the immediate blast radius substantially.

        Asking an Opus advisor to give a concrete, actionable design for stages 1-4 before writing code, given the correctness-criticality (this predictor's arithmetic has a documented history of contested spec ambiguities -- see jpxl_core::modular_weighted's EXPERIMENT_* constants) and the risk of quietly reintroducing an O(pixels) cost bloom into a search architecture Phase 4B just spent effort making sub-linear.
        """
    note """
        PROPOSED. Groundwork (shared jpxl_core::modular_weighted module) already landed and tested. This record captures the architecture complication found when starting the wiring step, pending advisor input on stages 1-4 above.
        """
    part_of [ @jpegxl-rs.track.encoder-optimization ]
    supported_by [ @jpegxl-rs.assessment.phase4-density-gap-is-vs-e7-only ]
}

record jpegxl-rs.work.arch-phase4b-sampled-gather-scoped/1 : work {
    title "Phase 4B: sampled property-gather to cut modular's dominant search-time cost"
    state completed
    intent """
        Now the priority sub-phase per jpegxl-rs.assessment.phase4-density-gap-is-vs-e7-only: the 4.0b real-corpus gate showed modular's dominant, unambiguous problem is wall-clock cost (100-120x versus cjxl -e1, at essentially identical output size), driven by the 67 full-plane cheap-tier residual scans per plan_for call (6 predictors x greedy split grid over SPLIT_PROPERTIES x SPLIT_THRESHOLDS + per-leaf refinement, crates/jpxl-encode/src/lossless.rs:154-248). Each scan re-walks the entire score plane (estimate_residual_bits_full) even though only a ranking decision, not an exact price, is needed at this stage.

        Goal: replace (or augment) the full-image cheap-tier scan with a sampled/summarized pass over the score planes that still ranks predictor/split candidates correctly, so plan_for's wall time scales with sample count, not pixel count, for the topology search.

        Safety model: this is Contract-A on the OUTPUT -- the existing exact final-price gate (lossless.rs:259-306, PriceTier::Exact) already re-prices the settled MA-tree winner exactly before it is adopted, so emitted bytes stay exactly priced regardless of how the search reached that candidate. The risk is purely a SEARCH-QUALITY one: does sampling ever change WHICH candidate the greedy search picks, in a way that leaves bytes on the table versus the full-scan search? That needs its own decision-preservation proof, echoing S8 Phase C's regret.rs independent-second-walk pattern (jpegxl-rs.work.arch-s8-full-redesign-scoped) -- a second, independent full-scan verification run on a held-out fixture set, not sharing code paths with the sampled scorer, checked against how often/how badly the sampled winner diverges from the full-scan winner.

        Scope, in order:
        1. Build the sampled gather as an ADDITIVE alternative scorer (new function alongside cheap_residual_bits, not a replacement) -- e.g. stratified or fixed-stride sample of rows/blocks, scaled Shannon-hybrid estimate.
        2. Prove on fixtures (small + the 4.0b real-corpus set) that sampled-winner selection matches full-scan selection within an explicit, named tolerance (bytes-left-on-table bound), using an independent second-walk harness.
        3. Wire behind a feature flag (following the s8-cover-prune pattern: off by default, diagnostics counters gated behind the same flag per jpegxl-rs.evidence.s8-phase-d-diagnostics-gated-verified's precedent).
        4. Measure wall-time win on the 4.0b corpus (0.8/4/12MP) with --diag; promote only if wall time drops materially with no exact-price regression (the Exact tier gate already prevents byte regression; this measures whether the search still finds equally-good candidates).

        Honest-negative-acceptable: if sampling changes winners too often, or the wall-time win doesn't materialize once Exact-tier re-pricing overhead is accounted for, it stays off -- same discipline as S8.

        Not in scope here: 4A (Weighted predictor) and 4C (global tree), which address the smaller, secondary vs-cjxl-e7-only density gap and are scoped separately once 4B lands or is honestly-negatived.
        """
    note """
        PROPOSED, not started. Opened per jpegxl-rs.assessment.phase4-density-gap-is-vs-e7-only's corrected order (4.0 -> 4.0b -> 4B -> 4A -> 4C -> 4D). This is now the next actionable engineering unit for Phase 4.
        """
    part_of [ @jpegxl-rs.track.encoder-optimization ]
    supported_by [
        @jpegxl-rs.assessment.phase4-density-gap-is-vs-e7-only,
        @jpegxl-rs.evidence.phase4-0b-density-gate-2026-08-08
    ]
}

record jpegxl-rs.work.arch-phase4c-global-ma-tree/1 : work {
    title "Phase 4C: emit one global MA tree (use_global_tree) instead of re-paying per section"
    state completed
    scope [
        path "JPXL/crates/jpxl-encode/src/lib.rs",
        path "JPXL/crates/jpxl-encode/src/lossless.rs",
        path "JPXL/crates/jpxl-encode/src/modular/mod.rs",
        path "JPXL/crates/jpxl-encode/tests/**"
    ]
    intent """
        Wire use_global_tree so the frame MA tree (and residual D bundle) is paid once at G.1.3 and multi-section modular streams reuse it, instead of write_ma_tree + full ANS tables in every LfGlobal/LfGroup/PassGroup section.

        plan_for already builds one tree per frame. Emission still hardcodes use_global_tree=false and G.1.3 have_global_tree=false (modular/mod.rs). Decoder already supports GlobalTree with GLOBAL_TREE_SHARES_DISTRIBUTIONS=true (shared residual histograms, per-section ANS restart).

        Primary win: multi-group tree/table re-pay, not deeper search. Defer histogram clustering (4C.2) unless measurement shows residual tables dominate re-pay after tree reuse.

        Gates: pixel-identity lossless roundtrip (jpxl-decode + djxl); multi-group size strictly smaller on at least one fixture; single-section non-regress or safe; promote default for multi-section if size wins.
        """
    acceptance {
        check multi-group-size {
            statement """
                At least one multi-group fixture is strictly smaller with global tree than with per-section trees; no multi-group fixture grows.
                """
            method command
            verified_by [ @jpegxl-rs.evidence.phase4c-multi-group-size-2026-08-12 ]
        }
        check pixel-identity {
            statement """
                Multi-group and single-group modular streams round-trip exact pixels through jpxl-decode; multi-group also through djxl when available.
                """
            method command
            verified_by [ @jpegxl-rs.evidence.phase4c-pixel-identity-2026-08-12 ]
        }
        check policy-decision {
            statement """
                Global tree is either default for multi-section modular emission or an explicit research flag with production default unchanged; decision recorded with size evidence.
                """
            method observation
            verified_by [ @jpegxl-rs.evidence.phase4c-policy-decision-2026-08-12 ]
        }
        check single-section-safe {
            statement """
                Single-section modular encode still decodes; size is not worse than pre-4C beyond a documented slack (prefer identical or smaller).
                """
            method command
            verified_by [ @jpegxl-rs.evidence.phase4c-pixel-identity-2026-08-12 ]
        }
    }
    depends_on [
        @jpegxl-rs.work.arch-phase4a-weighted-predictor-scoped,
        @jpegxl-rs.work.arch-phase4b-sampled-gather-scoped
    ]
    derived_from [ @jpegxl-rs.assessment.phase4-density-gap-is-vs-e7-only ]
    implements [
        @jpegxl-rs.decision.encoder-architecture-phases,
        @jpegxl-rs.policy.optimization-correctness-gates
    ]
    part_of [ @jpegxl-rs.track.encoder-optimization ]
}

record jpegxl-rs.work.arch-phase4d-lz77-search-align/1 : work {
    title "Phase 4D: align Exact-tier LZ77 pricing with emission; measure lookback"
    state completed
    scope [
        path "JPXL/crates/jpxl-encode/src/lossless.rs",
        path "JPXL/crates/jpxl-encode/src/modular/mod.rs",
        path "JPXL/crates/jpxl-encode/tests/**"
    ]
    intent """
        Close the modular residual LZ77 search/emission mismatch and finish the Phase 4
        optional LZ77 tail.

        Known gaps (from Phase 4A incidental finding and the original 4D scope):

        1. Search alignment (density): plan_for Exact-tier finalist pricing constructs
           ModularSource with allow_lz77=false, while final emission always uses true
           (lib.rs encode_codestream_with_plan). Ranking can miss modes that only win
           once residual LZ77 is priced (palette index runs are the documented case).
           Cheap-tier ranking stays LZ77-free (Shannon residual estimate; Exact re-prices
           finalists). Flip Exact finalists to allow_lz77=true so ranking matches the
           emit path.

        2. Lookback (speed/density, optional after measurement): greedy_lz77_events uses
           a 256-entry linear reverse scan (RESIDUAL_LZ77_LOOKBACK). Measure whether a
           hash-chain (same lookback, same greedy longest-match rule) is byte-identical
           and faster; separately measure whether a larger lookback shrinks streams under
           the optimization correctness gates (equal-or-better size if match set changes).

        Not on the wall-time hot path for plan_for cheap scans (phase4-order-correction);
        primary acceptance is density/ranking honesty and pixel identity, with speed as
        a secondary observation.

        Order: measure mismatch and lookback impact first; promote only what wins or is
        neutral on size with dual-oracle decode.
        """
    acceptance {
        check pixel-identity {
            statement """
                Lossless streams round-trip exact samples via jpxl-decode; djxl when
                available on PATH also matches source samples.
                """
            method command
            verified_by [ @jpegxl-rs.evidence.phase4d-pixel-identity-2026-08-12 ]
        }
        check policy-decision {
            statement """
                Production default either promotes the aligned Exact-tier LZ77 pricing
                (and any lookback change that won measurement) or records an honest
                negative; remaining deferred pieces named.
                """
            method observation
            verified_by [ @jpegxl-rs.evidence.phase4d-policy-decision-2026-08-12 ]
        }
        check search-lz77-aligned {
            statement """
                Exact-tier plan_for finalist pricing uses allow_lz77=true so residual
                stream costs match emission's LZ77 gate; documented with a fixture where
                misaligned search previously under-priced a non-LZ77 path or left size
                on the table.
                """
            method command
            verified_by [ @jpegxl-rs.evidence.phase4d-search-lz77-aligned-2026-08-12 ]
        }
        check size-non-regress {
            statement """
                Default and full-search modular encodes are no larger than pre-4D on the
                0.8/4/12MP photo corpus (and synthetic control fixtures); equal-or-smaller
                is the bar when lookback or ranking changes match sets.
                """
            method command
            verified_by [ @jpegxl-rs.evidence.phase4d-size-non-regress-2026-08-12 ]
        }
    }
    after [ @jpegxl-rs.work.arch-phase4c-global-ma-tree ]
    depends_on [ @jpegxl-rs.work.arch-phase4c-global-ma-tree ]
    part_of [ @jpegxl-rs.track.encoder-optimization ]
    supported_by [ @jpegxl-rs.assessment.phase4-order-correction ]
}

record jpegxl-rs.work.arch-phase4e-modular-effort-ramp/1 : work {
    title "Phase 4E: lossless modular effort ramp, then reoriented to a lean default (the search above e1 is chaff)"
    state completed
    scope [
        path "path \"JPXL/crates/jpxl-cli/**\"",
        path "path \"JPXL/crates/jpxl-encode/**\""
    ]
