record jpegxl-rs.work.arch-phase8-5-leaf-finishing/6 : work {
    title "Phase 8.5: profile-guided leaf and build optimization"
    state superseded
    scope [ path "JPXL/Cargo.toml", path "JPXL/crates/**" ]
    intent """
        After structural amplification is removed, reprofile and optimize only leaves at or above 5% of samples, then evaluate native CPU selection, LTO, PGO, allocator behavior, and hardware counters. Preserve scalar fallbacks and clean-room boundaries.
        """
    note """
        Fresh same-host Linux matched-quality timing replaces the prior cross-host projection. With the current byte-identical PGO binary, five alternating 4.3 MP pairs measure JPXL/cjxl medians 3044.438/505.132 ms (6.027x); three alternating unseen 12 MP pairs measure 5965.845/1305.590 ms (4.569x). SSIMULACRA2 deltas are 0.0979 and 0.1477, but JPXL is 14.69%/7.31% larger and its Butteraugli distance is 5.22%/60.37% worse, so this is primary-metric matching rather than multi-metric parity. The powersave-governor host and larger cjxl variance make this a diagnostic ratio, though alternating order and stable output hashes bound drift. Remaining parity requires 83.41%/78.12% runtime reductions. Keep Phase 8.5 active; the next boundary must be structural repeated-traversal reduction or coarse parallelism justified by a fresh >=5% profile, not another unprofiled leaf tweak.
        """
    acceptance {
        check profile-justified {
            statement """
                Every leaf change targets >=5% current samples and improves end-to-end.
                """
            method observation
            verified_by [
                @jpegxl-rs.evidence.phase8-5-linux-leaf-speed-2026-08-14/1,
                @jpegxl-rs.evidence.phase8-5-linux-profile-attribution-2026-08-14/1
            ]
        }
        check quality-preserved {
            statement """
                All decoder, target-rate, perceptual, thread-determinism gates pass.
                """
            method command
            verified_by [ @jpegxl-rs.evidence.phase8-5-linux-quality-2026-08-14/1 ]
        }
    }
    depends_on [ @jpegxl-rs.work.arch-phase8-4-finalist-token-tape ]
    part_of [ @jpegxl-rs.track.encoder-optimization ]
    supersedes [ @jpegxl-rs.work.arch-phase8-5-leaf-finishing/5 ]
}

record jpegxl-rs.work.arch-phase8-5-leaf-finishing/7 : work {
    title "Phase 8.5: profile-guided leaf and build optimization"
    state superseded
    scope [ path "JPXL/Cargo.toml", path "JPXL/crates/**" ]
    intent """
        After structural amplification is removed, reprofile and optimize only leaves at or above 5% of samples, then evaluate native CPU selection, LTO, PGO, allocator behavior, and hardware counters. Preserve scalar fallbacks and clean-room boundaries.
        """
    note """
        Retained the checked ties-away rounding leaf change at commit 7f6d90673ad604a2240ba5f35292387e7b13af2c after a fresh profile placed HF quantization at >=9.8%: median end-to-end time improved 3.18% on the mid image (5/5 paired wins) and 1.62% on the large image (2/3), cycles fell 2.68%, roundf disappeared, and all tested streams remained byte-identical. A fresh post-change PGO, matched-quality process-to-process matrix then established the architecture baseline: JPXL 1->4-thread speedup is 1.34x mid and 1.95x large versus cjxl 2.54x and 2.34x; JPXL/cjxl gaps are 3.02x/3.47x sequential and 5.71x/4.17x at four threads. Matching cjxl scaling alone would only restore the roughly 3.0-3.5x sequential gap, so parity requires both major sequential work reduction and finer-than-current-LF-group parallel work, especially for the mid-size case. The next checkpoint should split hot quantization/planning into more independent deterministic units or remove serial global work, then rerun this exact matrix. Saliency/AQ and raw-autotune scene semantics remain optional quality priors, not the primary parity architecture; raw-autotune must communicate through a neutral boundary because of its AGPL license.
        """
    acceptance {
        check profile-justified {
            statement """
                Every leaf change targets >=5% current samples and improves end-to-end.
                """
            method observation
            verified_by [
                @jpegxl-rs.evidence.phase8-5-linux-leaf-speed-2026-08-14/1,
                @jpegxl-rs.evidence.phase8-5-linux-profile-attribution-2026-08-14/1
            ]
        }
        check quality-preserved {
            statement """
                All decoder, target-rate, perceptual, thread-determinism gates pass.
                """
            method command
            verified_by [ @jpegxl-rs.evidence.phase8-5-linux-quality-2026-08-14/1 ]
        }
    }
    depends_on [ @jpegxl-rs.work.arch-phase8-4-finalist-token-tape ]
    part_of [ @jpegxl-rs.track.encoder-optimization ]
    supersedes [ @jpegxl-rs.work.arch-phase8-5-leaf-finishing/6 ]
}

