record jpegxl-rs.work.publish-readme-benchmark-mit/1 : work {
    title "Publish-ready README, reproducible libjxl comparison, and MIT-only licensing"
    state proposed
    scope [
        path "AGENTS.md",
        path "JPEG_XL_CLEAN_IMPLEMENTATION_LESSONS.md",
        path "JPXL/Cargo.toml",
        path "JPXL/LICENSE-MIT",
        path "JPXL/crates/jpxl-cli/**",
        path "JPXL/docs/experiments/**",
        path "JPXL/tools/**",
        path "LICENSE",
        path "README.md",
        path "RUST_JXL_ENCODER_ROADMAP.md",
        path "docs/generated/**"
    ]
    intent """
        Create a publish-ready repository surface: an accurate current-state README, a reproducible encoder quality-and-speed comparison with libjxl, MIT-only project licensing, and the local Git remote needed to publish the resulting verified work to LegeApp/JPXL.
        """
    acceptance {
        check comparison-reproducible {
            statement """
                A documented command produces a quality-and-speed comparison using JPXL and cjxl/djxl on the same inputs with recorded provenance.
                """
            method command
        }
        check mit-only {
            statement """
                Workspace package metadata and repository licensing surface declare MIT-only terms.
                """
            method command
        }
        check readme-current-state {
            statement """
                README accurately describes the supported scope, known exclusions, clean-room policy, build instructions, and the recorded benchmark.
                """
            method manual
        }
        check workspace-gates {
            statement """
                The required workspace build, test, lint, and formatting gates pass.
                """
            method command
        }
    }
}

record jpegxl-rs.work.quality-q0-harness-attribution/1 : work {
    title "Phase Q0: quality/density harness, section-byte attribution and the promotion bounds for the quality track"
    state completed
    scope [
        path ".agent/scratch/quality-track/**",
        path "JPXL/crates/jpxl-cli/src/main.rs",
        path "JPXL/crates/jpxl-encode-policy/src/lib.rs",
        path "JPXL/crates/jpxl-encode-policy/src/quantize.rs",
        path "JPXL/crates/jpxl-encode-policy/src/request.rs",
        path "JPXL/docs/optimize.md"
    ]
    intent """
        Speed is done (Phases 30-42: Balanced 15-25% faster than cjxl -e7 at SSIMULACRA2 parity, ~13% larger files). Open the quality/density track: (1) CLI research controls --dead-zone-scale (EncodeRequest.dead_zone_scale, default 1.0 = exact nearest rule, byte-identical), --tolerance, and --sections (per-SectionKind byte breakdown from CodestreamSizing); (2) a standing harness under .agent/scratch/quality-track/ (ladder.sh: mid/large/mid2 photo x 0.5/1/2 bpp x Fast/Balanced/Quality, djxl + jxl-oxide decodes, jpxl compare; scenes.sh: seven scenes at 1 bpp; cjxl-match.sh: cjxl -e7 -d bisected to matched bytes; summarise.py: deltas, BD-SSIM2/BD-rate, verdict); (3) attribution of the density gap by section bytes. First and decisive finding: --sections shows LF-group sections at ~38% of a 1 bpp VarDCT stream (mid 205 of 539 KB, large 567 of 1496 KB) because write_modular_stream coded every control image with a one-leaf tree and one flat prefix code; a temporary trace measured the metadata stream at 44.8 KB of tokens against 6.4 KB order-0 entropy and the LF planes at ~150 KB against ~114 KB. That lossless recoding is Phase Q0b (jpegxl-rs.work.quality-q0b-lf-group-entropy), funded before Q1; the remaining ablations (dead zone, quant_lf, QM scales, EPF, tolerance) move into Q1/Q2 as their own harness sweeps. Attribution written to .agent/scratch/quality-track/attribution.md; promotion bounds written into jpegxl-rs.decision.optimization-determinism-contract.
        """
    note """
        Opened and closed 2026-08-17 from the approved quality plan (Q0-Q4). Speed budget for the whole track: Balanced pinned wall <= +15% cumulative vs jpxl-p42d; Q0b spent about 9 points of it (instructions) / 4-6 points (quiet-host wall).
        """
    depends_on [ @jpegxl-rs.work.arch-phase42-writer-parallelism/1 ]
    part_of [ @jpegxl-rs.track.encoder-optimization ]
    verified_by [ @jpegxl-rs.evidence.q0-harness-and-sections-2026-08-17/1 ]
}

record jpegxl-rs.work.quality-q0b-lf-group-entropy/1 : work {
    title "Phase Q0b: entropy-code the LF-group control images (LF planes, CfL, BlockInfo, Sharpness) with per-channel ANS histograms and a bounded MA-tree context model"
    state completed
    scope [
        path ".agent/scratch/quality-track/**",
        path "JPXL/crates/jpxl-encode/src/modular/mod.rs",
        path "JPXL/crates/jpxl-encode/src/vardct/modular_out.rs",
        path "JPXL/crates/jpxl-encode/src/vardct/write.rs",
        path "JPXL/crates/jpxl-encode/tests/**",
        path "JPXL/docs/optimize.md"
    ]
    intent """
        Replace write_modular_stream's one-leaf tree + flat prefix code (H.2/H.4.2 minimal writer) with a real modular coder for VarDCT's control images: an MA tree whose root chain splits on the channel-index property so each channel owns its contexts, a bounded greedy learner over the static Table H.4 neighbourhood properties (|N|, |W|, west gradient error, W-NW, NW-N, N-NE, N-NN, W-WW; no property 15 so no self-correcting predictor is needed at the decoder) with a fixed threshold grid and a token-entropy price, and per-context ANS histograms with hybrid-uint configuration search (prefix codes tried where cheaper). Same decisions, same decoded pixels; fewer bytes. Under target-rate presets the rate loop hands the saved bytes to HF. Cost cap: the writer runs once per priced/stored codestream per LF group (about six times per Balanced encode), so learning is O(samples x properties) with small constants and the total Balanced wall stays inside the track's +15% budget; measured with the pinned sidecar. Gate: fixed-quantizer decode identity (pixels) through jpxl-decode, djxl and jxl-oxide; section bytes down; target-rate quality screen per Q0 bounds; 1-vs-4-thread hash equality.
        """
    note """
        Opened 2026-08-17 from Q0's first attribution finding. Not byte-identical by design (Contract A holds for pixels at fixed decisions, not bytes); the target-rate outputs change through the rate loop, so this lands under the Q0 quality screen. Follow-up question it opens: quant_lf 8 was promoted under the flat code's mispriced LF residuals and must be re-screened.
        """
    depends_on [ @jpegxl-rs.work.quality-q0-harness-attribution/1 ]
    part_of [ @jpegxl-rs.track.encoder-optimization ]
    verified_by [
        @jpegxl-rs.evidence.q0b-identity-safety-2026-08-17/1,
        @jpegxl-rs.evidence.q0b-quality-2026-08-17/1,
        @jpegxl-rs.evidence.q0b-speed-2026-08-17/1
    ]
}

record jpegxl-rs.work.quality-q1-quantizer/1 : work {
    title "Phase Q1: the HF quantizer under the quality harness — quant_lf re-screen, dead-zone and lambda sweeps, real-cost last-position truncation"
    state completed
    scope [
        path ".agent/scratch/quality-track/**",
        path "JPXL/crates/jpxl-cli/src/main.rs",
        path "JPXL/crates/jpxl-encode-policy/src/lib.rs",
        path "JPXL/crates/jpxl-encode-policy/src/quantize.rs",
        path "JPXL/crates/jpxl-encode-policy/src/rate.rs",
        path "JPXL/crates/jpxl-encode-policy/src/request.rs",
        path "JPXL/docs/optimize.md"
    ]
    intent """
        With the LF sections entropy-coded (Q0b) the ledger's own pointers became testable on the standing harness: (1) quant_lf 8, promoted in Phase 5G under the flat code's mispriced LF residuals, re-screened over {2,3,4,5,6,12,16,24}: 4 is the optimum and is now the target-rate default (SSIMULACRA2 +0.37 ladder / +0.67 scenes at equal bytes, 3-norm Butteraugli -3%; --quant-lf 8 reaches the old value); (2) the dead-zone scale (0.85-1.5) and lambda_scale (2-8) sweeps are flat or negative around the shipped values; (3) the trailing-truncation price (new --zero-token-bits, 0.5-3 bits) moves SSIMULACRA2 by +-0.05, so 7.1a's real-cost last-position model is not funded: the pass is insensitive to its price. Contract revised: the worst-cell Butteraugli bound now reads on the 3-norm after the max-norm was measured swinging +8% to +18% in single cells on otherwise-neutral settings.
        """
    note """
        Opened and closed 2026-08-17 after Q0/Q0b. Speed neutral (+0.2% instructions).
        """
    depends_on [ @jpegxl-rs.work.quality-q0b-lf-group-entropy/1 ]
    part_of [ @jpegxl-rs.track.encoder-optimization ]
    verified_by [
        @jpegxl-rs.evidence.q1-quant-lf-4-promotion-2026-08-17/1,
        @jpegxl-rs.evidence.q1-sweeps-2026-08-17/1
    ]
}

record jpegxl-rs.work.quality-q2-chroma-hf/1 : work {
    title "Phase Q2: chroma-HF allocation, EPF and rate-effort sweep under the remaining quality-track speed budget"
    state completed
    scope [
        path ".agent/scratch/quality-track/**",
        path "JPXL/crates/jpxl-cli/src/main.rs",
        path "JPXL/crates/jpxl-encode-policy/src/lib.rs",
        path "JPXL/crates/jpxl-encode-policy/src/request.rs",
        path "JPXL/crates/jpxl-encode-policy/tests/truncation_saving.rs",
        path "JPXL/docs/optimize.md"
    ]
    intent """
        Phase Q2 targets the remaining high-frequency red/green perceptual deficit recorded by Phase 8.6 and the Q0b matched-byte comparison, while deliberately spending only the quality track's remaining speed budget. Re-screen the already-wired X/B quant-matrix scales, active-EPF choices, and rate undershoot tolerance on the Phase Q1 standing harness. Start with one-knob Fast/Balanced sweeps, attribute channel and rate effects, then screen only justified combinations. Promote at most one target-rate default change if it passes the SSIMULACRA2-first Contract B bounds, remains within +15% cumulative Balanced cost versus Phase 42 (about nine points already spent by Q0b), is deterministic and independently decodable, and leaves the Phase Q1 behavior reachable by explicit flags. Honest negative results are acceptable and should close the corresponding lever rather than forcing a promotion.
        """
    note """
        Opened 2026-08-18 from the completed Q1 handoff and Q0's approved Q0-Q4 quality plan. Q1 closed quant_lf, dead-zone, lambda and truncation-price levers; Q2 owns the deferred QM/EPF/tolerance sweep and the red/green HF target. Scope now includes the Phase 7 truncation mechanism test because Q2's automatic chroma policy must be disabled there to preserve its single-variable invariant.
        """
    acceptance {
        check chroma-attribution {
            statement """
                The X/B QM, EPF, and undershoot-tolerance sweeps are recorded separately enough to attribute any quality gain; a promoted setting has an explicit per-channel/per-rate rationale rather than an unexplained bundle.
                """
            method observation
            verified_by [ @jpegxl-rs.evidence.quality-q2-chroma-attribution-2026-08-18/2 ]
        }
        check compatibility-control {
            statement """
                The previous Phase Q1 policy remains reachable through explicit CLI research controls and reproduces its retained codestream fingerprints on the canonical mid and large images.
                """
            method command
            verified_by [ @jpegxl-rs.evidence.quality-q2-compatibility-control-2026-08-18/2 ]
        }
        check determinism-decoders {
            statement """
                Promoted target-rate outputs are byte-identical across one and four threads and with AVX2 disabled, and representative/corpus streams are accepted by djxl and jxl-oxide.
                """
            method command
            verified_by [ @jpegxl-rs.evidence.quality-q2-determinism-decoders-2026-08-18/2 ]
        }
        check gates {
            statement """
                Workspace formatting, build, tests, strict Clippy, no-default-features checks, and AKR validation pass, or any unchanged pre-existing diagnostic is explicitly retained with raw output.
                """
            method command
            verified_by [ @jpegxl-rs.evidence.quality-q2-rust-gates-2026-08-18/2 ]
        }
        check quality-gate {
            statement """
                The promoted Q2 candidate passes the standing ladder and seven-scene Contract B gate against the Phase Q1 binary: SSIMULACRA2 mean delta is non-negative with no cell below -0.5, Butteraugli max-norm mean is no worse than +2%, Butteraugli pnorm3 has no cell worse than +5%, and matched-SSIMULACRA2 bytes do not increase.
                """
            method observation
            verified_by [ @jpegxl-rs.evidence.quality-q2-corpus-gates-2026-08-18/2 ]
        }
        check speed-budget {
            statement """
                Pinned four-worker Balanced timing or instruction-count evidence keeps the cumulative quality-track cost within +15% of the Phase 42 binary, with the already-spent Q0b cost included.
                """
            method command
            verified_by [ @jpegxl-rs.evidence.quality-q2-speed-budget-2026-08-18/1 ]
        }
    }
    depends_on [ @jpegxl-rs.work.quality-q1-quantizer/1 ]
    part_of [ @jpegxl-rs.track.encoder-optimization/1 ]
}

record jpegxl-rs.work.quality-q3-ladder-ceiling-and-allocation-screens/1 : work {
    title "Phase Q3: rate-ladder ceiling fix; fine-lattice AQ, adaptive EPF, size-penalty and X-scale screens"
    state completed
    scope [
        path ".agent/scratch/q3/**",
        path ".agent/scratch/quality-track/**",
        path "JPXL/crates/jpxl-cli/src/main.rs",
        path "JPXL/crates/jpxl-encode-policy/src/field.rs",
        path "JPXL/crates/jpxl-encode-policy/src/lib.rs",
        path "JPXL/crates/jpxl-encode-policy/src/rate.rs",
        path "JPXL/crates/jpxl-encode-policy/src/request.rs",
        path "JPXL/crates/jpxl-encode-policy/tests/truncation_saving.rs",
        path "JPXL/docs/experiments/2026-08-18-q3-fine-lattice-aq-and-adaptive-epf.md",
        path "JPXL/docs/optimize.md"
    ]
    intent """
        Phase Q3 asks how far the Phase Q2 encoder is from cjxl -e 7 at matched bytes on every standing metric, localises the remaining Butteraugli deficit spatially, and screens the per-block allocation levers that could close it inside the quality track's remaining +6 points of Balanced speed budget: adaptive quantization on a sixteenth-octave HfMul lattice (eroded masking, uniform, edge-adjacent refinement), an activity-adaptive EPF sharpness plane, and re-screens of the Phase 6.2b size penalty and X quant-matrix scale 3 on the standing corpus. Promote only what passes the Contract B bounds; record honest negatives per lever. Fix any rate-control defect the standing harness exposes on the way.
        """
    note """
        Opened 2026-08-18 from the completed Q2 handoff. The first standing measurement exposed a rate-control defect rather than an allocation one: above the global_scale ceiling the ladder stepped by whole HfMul multiples, so mid2 at 2 bpp emitted 698 KB for a 1,080 KB target and large at 2 bpp 2.18 MB for 3.0 MB, 'budget spent, not at the ladder's limit'. That fix (dense HfMul x global_scale segments with quant_lf coupled up to 16) is the pass's promoted change; every allocation lever screened negative and is retained as a documented research control. Measurements were taken on a clean git worktree at 13498bb plus this pass's patch because another agent was concurrently editing jpxl-encode (16-bit input work) in the main worktree.
        """
    acceptance {
        check allocation-screens-recorded {
            statement """
                Each screened allocation lever (fine-masking, fine-uniform, edge-refine fields; adaptive EPF sharpness; size penalty measured/custom; X scale 3) has its result recorded with raw numbers, and none is promoted without passing the corpus bounds.
                """
            method observation
            verified_by [ @jpegxl-rs.evidence.quality-q3-allocation-screens-2026-08-18/1 ]
        }
        check determinism-decoders {
            statement """
                Changed target-rate outputs are byte-identical across one and four threads, and every changed stream decodes in djxl and jxl-oxide.
                """
            method command
            verified_by [ @jpegxl-rs.evidence.quality-q3-determinism-decoders-2026-08-18/2 ]
        }
        check gates {
            statement """
                cargo fmt --check, clippy -D warnings, the full workspace test suite (Windows fixture links materialised, JPXL_DISABLE_AVX2=1 as in Q2), and the no-default-features check pass on a clean worktree carrying only this pass's patch.
                """
            method command
            verified_by [ @jpegxl-rs.evidence.quality-q3-rust-gates-2026-08-18/2 ]
        }
        check ladder-ceiling-fix {
            statement """
                Target-rate encodes whose crossing lies above the global_scale ceiling reach their byte target within the preset tolerance instead of undershooting: mid2 2 bpp Balanced emits within 0.1% of 1,080,000 bytes and large 2 bpp within 0.1% of 3,000,000 bytes, and cells below the ceiling keep their Phase Q2 codestream hashes.
                """
            method command
            command "bash .agent/scratch/quality-track/q3-arm.sh q3-final"
            verified_by [ @jpegxl-rs.evidence.quality-q3-ladder-ceiling-fix-2026-08-18/2 ]
        }
        check quality-gate {
            statement """
                The final binary passes the standing ladder and seven-scene Contract B gate against the Phase Q2 outputs: SSIMULACRA2 mean delta non-negative with no cell below -0.5, Butteraugli max-norm mean no worse than +2%, no 3-norm cell worse than +5%, every stream accepted by djxl and jxl-oxide; the only changed cells are the ceiling-bound ones and they improve.
                """
            method observation
            verified_by [ @jpegxl-rs.evidence.quality-q3-corpus-gates-2026-08-18/2 ]
        }
        check speed-budget {
            statement """
                Alternating native Windows A/B timing on the standing mid 1 bpp Balanced cell keeps the cumulative quality-track cost within +15% of Phase 42: the Q3 binary is within noise of the frozen Phase Q1 binary.
                """
            method command
            verified_by [ @jpegxl-rs.evidence.quality-q3-speed-budget-2026-08-18/2 ]
        }
    }
    depends_on [ @jpegxl-rs.work.quality-q2-chroma-hf/1 ]
    part_of [ @jpegxl-rs.track.encoder-optimization/1 ]
}

record jpegxl-rs.work.quality-q4-cover-rate-model/1 : work {
    title "Phase Q4: audit and calibrate the cover objective's rate proxy against the writer's actual token costs"
    state completed
    scope [
        path ".agent/scratch/quality-track/**",
        path "JPXL/crates/jpxl-cli/src/main.rs",
        path "JPXL/crates/jpxl-encode-policy/src/lib.rs",
        path "JPXL/crates/jpxl-encode-policy/src/request.rs",
        path "JPXL/crates/jpxl-encode-policy/tests/rate_proxy_audit.rs",
        path "JPXL/crates/jpxl-encode/src/vardct/sink.rs",
        path "JPXL/crates/jpxl-encode/src/vardct/walk.rs",
        path "JPXL/docs/optimize.md"
    ]
    intent """
        Q3 identified the cover's merge decisions as the one lever that moves PSNR and Butteraugli together. Q4 measures how the cover objective's rate proxy (bitlen+1 per nonzero, zeros free, 2 bits per varblock, 32 per merged transform) compares with what the writer actually spends per varblock and per transform size, by walking the chosen plan with a costing HfEventSink under its own trained histograms; derives per-size residual scales and per-varblock fixed bits from that audit; screens the calibrated model (and a size-ordering-only variant) on the standing corpus against Phase Q3; and promotes it only if it improves SSIMULACRA2 and Butteraugli together (the operator's rule: a seesaw against SSIMULACRA2 is not accepted).
        """
    note """
        Opened 2026-08-18 after Q3. The audit needed a no-op varblock(transform, hf_mul) hook on HfEventSink (jpxl-encode). Calibrated constants come from the mid photo at 1 bpp; the same ordering holds on large and mid2. Promoted as the target-rate default; the fixed-quantizer defaults keep the legacy proxy so Contract A fingerprints do not move; --cover-rate-model legacy reproduces the Q3 streams.
        """
    acceptance {
        check audit-recorded {
            statement """
                The rate-proxy audit reports, per transform size, actual bits versus proxy bits and the split into non_zeros symbols, nonzero tokens and interior-zero tokens on the three standing photos, and the calibrated constants are derived from it.
                """
            method command
            command "JPXL_RATE_AUDIT_PPM=<ppm> cargo test -p jpxl-encode-policy --profile fast-debug --test rate_proxy_audit -- --ignored --nocapture"
            verified_by [ @jpegxl-rs.evidence.quality-q4-rate-audit-2026-08-18/1 ]
        }
        check compatibility-determinism {
            statement """
                --cover-rate-model legacy reproduces the Phase Q3 hashes, the fixed-quantizer defaults keep the legacy proxy, and promoted outputs are byte-identical across one and four threads.
                """
            method command
            verified_by [
                @jpegxl-rs.evidence.quality-q4-compatibility-determinism-2026-08-18/2
            ]
        }
        check gates {
            statement """
                cargo fmt --check, clippy -D warnings, the full workspace test suite (Windows fixture links, JPXL_DISABLE_AVX2=1) and the no-default-features check pass.
                """
            method command
            verified_by [ @jpegxl-rs.evidence.quality-q4-rust-gates-2026-08-18/2 ]
        }
        check quality-gate {
            statement """
                The calibrated rate model passes the standing ladder and seven-scene Contract B gate against Phase Q3 with SSIMULACRA2 mean and Butteraugli 3-norm mean both improving (no seesaw), every stream accepted by djxl and jxl-oxide.
                """
            method observation
            verified_by [ @jpegxl-rs.evidence.quality-q4-corpus-gates-2026-08-18/2 ]
        }
        check speed-budget {
            statement """
                Alternating A/B timing of the calibrated model against legacy is neutral on the standing mid 1 bpp and large 1 bpp Balanced cells.
                """
            method command
            verified_by [ @jpegxl-rs.evidence.quality-q4-speed-budget-2026-08-18/2 ]
        }
    }
    depends_on [ @jpegxl-rs.work.quality-q3-ladder-ceiling-and-allocation-screens/1 ]
    part_of [ @jpegxl-rs.track.encoder-optimization/1 ]
}

record jpegxl-rs.work.quality-q5-anchored-controller-above-ceiling/1 : work {
    title "Phase Q5: anchored-controller fixes above the ceiling (second-anchor exponent, structure rebuild, second correction) — screened, mechanism kept, legacy defaults retained"
    state completed
    scope [
        path ".agent/scratch/quality-track/**",
        path "JPXL/crates/jpxl-cli/src/main.rs",
        path "JPXL/crates/jpxl-encode-policy/src/rate.rs",
        path "JPXL/docs/optimize.md"
    ]
    intent """
        Fix the Q3 speed follow-up (Balanced falls back to the exhaustive controller above the global_scale ceiling: 5.9 s on mid2 at 2 bpp) by improving the two-anchor controller: a lower second-anchor exponent, a structure rebuild at the second anchor when the first anchor is far from the target, and a bounded second exact correction aimed with the local slope; also screen a fresh structural finalist. Promote only if the standing corpus stays within Contract B against Phase Q4; otherwise keep the mechanism as documented constants at their legacy values.
        """
    note """
        Screened 2026-08-18. The second correction removes every fallback on the standing corpus (mid2 2 bpp Balanced 5.9 s -> 0.78 s), but the fallback had been a hidden quality tier (fresh cover/CfL/entropy per probe), so the cells that used to fall back drop to their true Fast/Balanced tier: mid2 2 bpp Balanced -0.25 SSIMULACRA2, the 20240503_105759 scene at Fast -4.0, failing the Contract B worst-cell bound. Under the quality-first rule the defaults stay legacy (exponent 2.0, no rebuild, one correction) and the constants document the screen; the next controller item is a cheaper fresh-structure fallback seeded from the anchors. Committed state is byte-identical to Phase Q4.
        """
    acceptance {
        check gates {
            statement """
                cargo fmt --check, clippy -D warnings and the encode-policy suite pass on the committed state.
                """
            method command
            verified_by [ @jpegxl-rs.evidence.quality-q5-rust-gates-2026-08-18/1 ]
        }
        check screen-recorded {
            statement """
                The three controller changes and the fresh-finalist variant are screened on the standing corpus against Phase Q4 with per-cell numbers, the fallback-as-hidden-tier finding is documented, and the committed defaults reproduce the Phase Q4 hashes.
                """
            method command
            verified_by [ @jpegxl-rs.evidence.quality-q5-controller-screen-2026-08-18/2 ]
        }
    }
    depends_on [ @jpegxl-rs.work.quality-q4-cover-rate-model/1 ]
    part_of [ @jpegxl-rs.track.encoder-optimization/1 ]
}

record jpegxl-rs.work.quality-q6-cheaper-exhaustive-search/1 : work {
    title "Phase Q6: cheaper fresh-structure exhaustive search — local navigation bracket, seeded fallback, fill only outside the tolerance band"
    state completed
    scope [
        path ".agent/scratch/quality-track/**",
        path "JPXL/crates/jpxl-encode-policy/src/rate.rs",
        path "JPXL/crates/jpxl-encode-policy/tests/rate_loop.rs",
        path "JPXL/docs/optimize.md"
    ]
    intent """
        Take the speed side of Q5's finding without giving up the fallback's fresh structure: make the exhaustive controller (Quality preset and Fast/Balanced fallbacks) spend fewer prices for the same landing. Bracket locally when the start is known to be near the crossing (Full-refinement navigation from the Fast winner; a fallback seeded with the anchored attempt's crossing estimate), extrapolate the exact correction along the navigation slope when its short bracket lacks a far point, and run the discrete notch fill only when the incumbent is still outside the tolerance band. Promote if the standing corpus stays within Contract B against Q4 and the price counts drop.
        """
    note """
        Screened and promoted 2026-08-18. Fast/Balanced cells that do not fall back are byte-identical to Q4; Quality cells and fallback cells move within noise (photos +0.003 / -0.06, scenes +0.015 / +0.00). Exhaustive-path prices: mid 1 bpp Quality 20 -> 12, large 0.5 bpp Quality 21 -> 13, mid2 2 bpp Quality 23 -> 15, mid2 2 bpp Balanced fallback 26 -> 12, the 20240503_105759 scene at Fast 25 -> 5; A/B against the Phase Q3 controller: Quality mid 1 bpp 3.9 -> 2.5 s, large 0.5 bpp 6.8 -> 4.7 s, mid2 2 bpp 6.5 -> 4.6 s, fallback 6.3 -> 4.9 s, scene Fast 1.93 -> 0.59 s.
        """
    acceptance {
        check determinism-gates {
            statement """
                One- and four-thread outputs are byte-identical on a Quality cell and a fallback cell; cargo fmt --check, clippy -D warnings and the encode-policy suite (including the rate-loop fixtures) pass.
                """
            method command
            verified_by [ @jpegxl-rs.evidence.quality-q6-determinism-gates-2026-08-18/1 ]
        }
        check price-reduction {
            statement """
                Exhaustive-path price counts and alternating A/B wall time drop on Quality cells and on the fallback cells, with raw traces and timings retained.
                """
            method command
            verified_by [ @jpegxl-rs.evidence.quality-q6-price-reduction-2026-08-18/1 ]
        }
        check quality-gate {
            statement """
                Against Phase Q4 the standing photo ladder and seven-scene screen stay within Contract B (SSIMULACRA2 mean non-negative, worst above -0.5, Butteraugli max-norm mean within +2%, 3-norm worst within +5%), every stream accepted by djxl and jxl-oxide, and Fast/Balanced non-fallback cells are byte-identical.
                """
            method observation
            verified_by [ @jpegxl-rs.evidence.quality-q6-corpus-gates-2026-08-18/2 ]
        }
    }
    depends_on [ @jpegxl-rs.work.quality-q5-anchored-controller-above-ceiling/1 ]
    part_of [ @jpegxl-rs.track.encoder-optimization/1 ]
}

record jpegxl-rs.work.quality-q7-effective-scale-controller/1 : work {
    title "Phase Q7: effective-scale cold bracketing, duplicate-price suppression, bounded Quality top-off, and exact saturation reporting"
    state completed
    scope [
        path ".agent/scratch/quality-track/**",
        path "JPXL/crates/jpxl-encode-policy/src/rate.rs",
        path "JPXL/crates/jpxl-encode-policy/tests/rate_loop.rs",
        path "JPXL/docs/optimize.md"
    ]
    intent """
        Continue the diminishing-returns quality/speed pass in the exact target-rate controller. Make Cold bracketing geometric in the ladder's true effective scale across the dense post-ceiling HfMul segments, suppress repeated exact prices of an already-seen rung without changing trace order or the hard budget, and report saturation when the top rung was actually priced feasible even if entropy non-monotonicity leaves a closer coarser incumbent. Reinvest at most one already-budgeted exact price for post-ceiling Quality finalists on frames up to 5 MP, while larger frames retain the requested tolerance as their stop. Preserve every public entry point and the never-over, representable-rung, deterministic tie-break, non-monotone-pocket, and error-propagation contracts. Promote only if corpus quality stays within Contract B and exhaustive high-rate price counts and wall time improve.
        """
    note """
        Screened candidate passes the 27-cell photo ladder and 14-cell scene gate against Phase Q6. Only two 2 bpp Quality cells change; high-rate Quality price counts fall 12->10, 15->14, and 11->7 on mid/mid2/large, with alternating medians -30.8%, -4.2%, and -28.8%.
        """
    acceptance {
        check controller-invariants {
            statement """
                Rate-loop tests cover effective-scale stepping across the ceiling, duplicate-price suppression, floor/top and saturated edge cases, hard-budget accounting, and existing non-monotone behavior; all pass.
                """
            method command
            command "cargo test -p jpxl-encode-policy --lib rate::tests --profile fast-debug"
            verified_by [ @jpegxl-rs.evidence.quality-q7-controller-invariants-2026-08-18/1 ]
        }
        check corpus-gate {
            statement """
                The standing photo ladder and scene screen remain within Contract B against Phase Q6, with decoder acceptance intact.
                """
            method observation
            verified_by [ @jpegxl-rs.evidence.quality-q7-corpus-gates-2026-08-18/1 ]
        }
        check price-reduction {
            statement """
                At least one standing exhaustive high-rate cell uses fewer exact prices or lower interleaved wall time without a material quality regression.
                """
            method observation
            verified_by [ @jpegxl-rs.evidence.quality-q7-price-and-speed-2026-08-18/1 ]
        }
        check workspace-gates {
            statement """
                Workspace build, tests, strict Clippy, and formatting pass under the pinned toolchain.
                """
            method command
            command "cargo build --workspace && cargo test --workspace --profile fast-debug && cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings && cargo fmt --all --check"
            verified_by [ @jpegxl-rs.evidence.quality-q7-workspace-gates-2026-08-18/1 ]
        }
    }
    depends_on [ @jpegxl-rs.work.quality-q6-cheaper-exhaustive-search/1 ]
    implements [ @jpegxl-rs.decision.optimization-determinism-contract/1 ]
    part_of [ @jpegxl-rs.track.encoder-optimization/1 ]
}

record jpegxl-rs.work.quality-q8-chroma-allocation/1 : work {
    title "Phase Q8: graduate the Quality-only chroma QM allocation — B=4 above 1 bpp and X=3 at or below it"
    state completed
    scope [
        path ".agent/scratch/quality-track/**",
        path "JPXL/crates/jpxl-cli/src/main.rs",
        path "JPXL/crates/jpxl-encode-policy/src/lib.rs",
        path "JPXL/crates/jpxl-encode-policy/src/request.rs",
        path "JPXL/docs/optimize.md"
    ]
    intent """
        Extend the promoted Phase Q2 Quality-only chroma refinement to the two surfaces it left neutral, where the rate ladder was undershooting the byte target and leaving chroma bits unspent: the B channel above 1 bpp (scale 4, since Q2's B=5 there overshot the Butteraugli 3-norm bound) and the X channel at or below 1 bpp (scale 3). The policy stays confined to the exhaustive Quality preset, so Fast, Balanced, the seven-scene screen, and every fixed-quantizer stream remain byte-identical; rename ChromaHfPolicy::QualityLowRateB5 to QualityChroma, graduate effective_b_qm_scale across the 1 bpp boundary, add a mirroring effective_x_qm_scale, and make the CLI pin Manual for an explicit --x-qm-scale so a research override still wins. Promote only if the standing photo ladder and seven-scene screen pass the Contract B bounds against the frozen Phase Q7 binary with both decoders accepting every changed stream.
        """
    note """
        Screened candidate passes both standing corpora against Q7: photo ladder SSIMULACRA2 mean +0.038 / worst -0.026, Butteraugli max mean -0.26% (improves) / 3-norm worst +3.12%; scenes byte-identical. Only the nine Quality photo cells change; compiled policy reproduces the manual-flag sweep bit-for-bit at one and four threads. Headline cell mid 2 bpp Quality +0.586 SSIMULACRA2 at -0.3% Butteraugli max.
        """
    acceptance {
        check byte-identity {
            statement """
                Fast, Balanced, and every fixed-quantizer stream stay byte-identical to Phase Q7; the compiled Quality policy reproduces the equivalent manual-flag streams, and the changed Quality cells are byte-identical at one and four threads.
                """
            method observation
            verified_by [ @jpegxl-rs.evidence.quality-q8-byte-identity-2026-08-18/1 ]
        }
        check corpus-gate {
            statement """
                The standing photo ladder and seven-scene screen pass the Contract B bounds against the frozen Phase Q7 binary, with djxl and jxl-oxide accepting every changed Quality stream.
                """
            method observation
            verified_by [ @jpegxl-rs.evidence.quality-q8-corpus-gate-2026-08-18/1 ]
        }
        check policy-invariants {
            statement """
                Policy unit tests cover the rate-graduated Quality chroma scales (B 5->4 across 1 bpp, X 3 at or below it), Quality-only confinement for both channels at every rate, and Manual bypass for both channels; all pass.
                """
            method command
            command "cargo test -p jpxl-encode-policy --lib request:: --profile fast-debug"
            verified_by [ @jpegxl-rs.evidence.quality-q8-policy-invariants-2026-08-18/1 ]
        }
        check workspace-gates {
            statement """
                Workspace build, the full test suite, strict Clippy, and formatting pass under the pinned toolchain; the only test failures are the pre-existing host-dependent AVX2-fallback ULP checks in jpxl-core, which this change does not touch and which pass with the AVX2 fallback disabled.
                """
            method command
            command "cargo build --workspace && cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings && cargo fmt --all --check"
            verified_by [ @jpegxl-rs.evidence.quality-q8-workspace-gates-2026-08-18/1 ]
        }
    }
    depends_on [ @jpegxl-rs.work.quality-q7-effective-scale-controller/1 ]
    implements [
        @jpegxl-rs.decision.optimization-determinism-contract/1,
        @jpegxl-rs.decision.ssimulacra2-is-the-primary-promotion-metric/1
    ]
    part_of [ @jpegxl-rs.track.encoder-optimization/1 ]
}

record jpegxl-rs.work.quality-q8-preserve-chroma-policy-api/1 : work {
    title "Q8 follow-up: preserve the public ChromaHfPolicy variant spelling"
    state completed
    scope [ path "JPXL/crates/jpxl-encode-policy/src/request.rs", path "JPXL/docs/optimize.md" ]
    intent """
        Repair the source-compatibility regression introduced when Phase Q8 renamed the public ChromaHfPolicy::QualityLowRateB5 enum variant. Retain the historical variant as the actual enum discriminant, expose QualityChroma as a descriptive associated-constant alias for new code and documentation, keep the graduated Q8 X/B behavior and all codestream outputs unchanged, and correct the Q8 optimization note to describe the compatibility alias accurately. Add tests pinning both spellings and exhaustive matching through the legacy variant.
        """
    acceptance {
        check legacy-source-compatibility {
            statement """
                Tests compile and exercise ChromaHfPolicy::QualityLowRateB5, prove it equals the QualityChroma alias, and preserve exhaustive matching over the historical enum variants.
                """
            method command
            command "cargo test -p jpxl-encode-policy --lib request:: --profile fast-debug"
            verified_by [ @jpegxl-rs.evidence.quality-q8-api-compatibility-2026-08-18/1 ]
        }
        check output-identity {
            statement """
                Representative Q8 Quality outputs retain their pre-fix hashes and Fast/Balanced remain byte-identical to the frozen Q7 baseline.
                """
            method observation
            verified_by [ @jpegxl-rs.evidence.quality-q8-api-output-identity-2026-08-18/1 ]
        }
        check workspace-gates {
            statement """
                Workspace build, strict Clippy, formatting, and the full workspace/oracle suite pass under the established Windows AVX2 workaround.
                """
            method command
            command "cargo build --workspace && cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings && cargo fmt --all --check"
            verified_by [ @jpegxl-rs.evidence.quality-q8-api-workspace-gates-2026-08-18/1 ]
        }
    }
    depends_on [ @jpegxl-rs.work.quality-q8-chroma-allocation/1 ]
    implements [ @jpegxl-rs.decision.optimization-determinism-contract/1 ]
    part_of [ @jpegxl-rs.track.encoder-optimization/1 ]
}

record jpegxl-rs.work.quality-q9-production-presets/1 : work {
    title "Phase Q9: make Balanced the production default and promote Balanced-only chroma refinement"
    state completed
    scope [
        path ".agent/scratch/quality-track/**",
        path "JPXL/crates/jpxl-cli/src/main.rs",
        path "JPXL/crates/jpxl-conformance/tests/corpus.rs",
        path "JPXL/crates/jpxl-core/src/color.rs",
        path "JPXL/crates/jpxl-core/src/simd.rs",
        path "JPXL/crates/jpxl-encode-policy/src/rate.rs",
        path "JPXL/crates/jpxl-encode-policy/src/request.rs",
        path "JPXL/crates/jpxl-encode-policy/tests/rate_loop.rs",
        path "JPXL/docs/CONFORMANCE.md",
        path "JPXL/docs/optimize.md",
        path "JPXL/tools/materialize-conformance-links.ps1",
        path "README.md"
    ]
    intent """
        Act on the production-preset clarification by making Balanced, not exhaustive Quality, the default target-rate preset and by promoting the strongest zero-search-cost chroma candidate measured on the current Q8 head: X=3 and B=3 for automatic Balanced target-rate requests at every screened rate. Preserve explicit Quality as the exhaustive reference path, preserve Fast and fixed-quantizer outputs, preserve the historical ChromaHfPolicy enum variant and aliases, add a descriptive preset-wide alias without adding an enum discriminant, and keep explicit manual QM controls authoritative. Build and screen only with native Windows binaries and PowerShell harnesses. Repair the stale Windows AVX2/scalar cbrt mismatch with a shared software-defined operation, materialize Windows conformance link placeholders natively, and preserve the request-scoped inverse-Gaborish invariant when the now-default Balanced controller falls back to exhaustive search by sharing the already-preconditioned transform frame across both controller stages.
        """
    note """
        The quality, timing, and dispatch gates pass. Exact workspace testing then exposed two native-Windows/default-path setup defects: bike_5 had one materializable IntxLNK reference placeholder, and Balanced fallback rebuilt inverse-Gaborish so RateProbeStats reported two request-scoped preconditions. Both are direct efficiency/testability follow-ups, not changes to the promoted chroma decision.
        """
    acceptance {
        check determinism {
            statement """
                Changed Balanced outputs are byte-identical at one and four threads and the Windows non-AVX2 workspace tests pass.
                """
            method command
            verified_by [ @jpegxl-rs.evidence.quality-q9-determinism-2026-08-19/1 ]
        }
        check preset-scope {
            statement """
                The compiled automatic policy reproduces manual X=3/B=3 for Balanced, while Fast, explicit Quality, manual-QM requests, and fixed-quantizer outputs remain byte-identical to Q8 where claimed.
                """
            method command
            verified_by [ @jpegxl-rs.evidence.quality-q9-preset-scope-2026-08-19/1 ]
        }
        check production-default {
            statement """
                Default target-rate requests and the CLI select Balanced, while explicit Quality and Fast remain selectable and Quality still enters the exhaustive reference controller.
                """
            method observation
            verified_by [ @jpegxl-rs.evidence.quality-q9-production-default-2026-08-19/1 ]
        }
        check quality-gate {
            statement """
                The full standing native-Windows 27-photo-cell plus 14-scene-cell screen passes Contract B against the frozen Q8 binary, with djxl and jxl-oxide accepting every changed stream.
                """
            method command
            verified_by [ @jpegxl-rs.evidence.quality-q9-quality-screen-2026-08-19/1 ]
        }
        check speed-budget {
            statement """
                Native-Windows interleaved timing shows no material Balanced regression and remains inside the cumulative +15% quality-track budget.
                """
            method command
            verified_by [ @jpegxl-rs.evidence.quality-q9-speed-2026-08-19/1 ]
        }
        check workspace-gates {
            statement """
                cargo build --workspace, cargo test --workspace, cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings, and cargo fmt --all --check pass on Windows.
                """
            method command
            verified_by [ @jpegxl-rs.evidence.quality-q9-workspace-gates-2026-08-19/1 ]
        }
    }
    depends_on [ @jpegxl-rs.work.quality-q8-preserve-chroma-policy-api/1 ]
    implements [
        @jpegxl-rs.decision.lossy-production-presets/1,
        @jpegxl-rs.decision.optimization-determinism-contract/1,
        @jpegxl-rs.decision.ssimulacra2-is-the-primary-promotion-metric/1
    ]
    part_of [ @jpegxl-rs.track.encoder-optimization/1 ]
}

record jpegxl-rs.work.retire-handoff-ledger/1 : work {
    title "Retire HANDOFF.md as a duplicate ledger after AKR migration"
    state completed
    scope [
        path "AGENTS.md",
        path "JPXL/docs/CHANGELOG.md",
        path "JPXL/docs/HANDOFF.md",
        path "JPXL/docs/PLAN.md"
    ]
    intent """
        Complete the migration already declared by jpegxl-rs.decision.ledger-conventions: AKR records and generated views are the only live planning/handoff surface. The HANDOFF permanent sections have been audited: read_u32 wrapping, XYB inverse matrix, quant-bias defaults, modular LZ77 distance multiplier, asymmetric H.5.2 clamp, restoration filters off, E.4.4 tag count, modular 16-bit buffers, transcription-pipeline escalation, Annex H constants, C.2.6 alias mapping, and oracle output format all have matching decision or policy records. Replace the 2,185-line duplicate ledger with a short legacy tombstone, update contributor and changelog instructions to point to AKR/generated views, and preserve historical detail through Git history and the migrated records. Frozen experiment reports are not edited; the tombstone explains that their historical HANDOFF references resolve through Git history.
        """
    acceptance {
        check durable-facts-in-akr {
            statement """
                Every permanent Already-fixed/Trap item in HANDOFF.md has a corresponding AKR decision or policy record.
                """
            method observation
            verified_by [ @jpegxl-rs.evidence.retire-handoff-durable-facts-2026-08-11/1 ]
        }
        check legacy-tombstone-only {
            statement """
                JPXL/docs/HANDOFF.md is a concise legacy redirect rather than a second plan, experiment database, or dated work ledger.
                """
            method command
            command "wc -l JPXL/docs/HANDOFF.md"
            verified_by [ @jpegxl-rs.evidence.retire-handoff-tombstone-2026-08-11/1 ]
        }
        check no-live-handoff-workflow {
            statement """
                Contributor and changelog instructions no longer direct work-in-progress or handoff updates into HANDOFF.md; remaining HANDOFF references are the legacy tombstone or frozen historical experiment citations.
                """
            method command
            command "rg -n 'HANDOFF.md|HANDOFF' AGENTS.md JPXL/docs --glob '*.md'"
            verified_by [ @jpegxl-rs.evidence.retire-handoff-no-live-workflow-2026-08-11/1 ]
        }
    }
    implements [ @jpegxl-rs.decision.ledger-conventions/1 ]
}
